{
  "note": [
    "The pin that keeps ONE signed-edit decision honest across two",
    "implementations: engine/incremental.signed_edit_decision (the headless",
    "arm, which has no dialog to ask with) and renderer/lib/signatures.ts",
    "signedEditDecision (the surfaces that do). Read by",
    "tests/test_signed_edit.py and tests/signed-edit-corpus.test.ts, which",
    "must agree case for case.",
    "",
    "`policy` is what signature_policy reports. `reason` is a stable enum",
    "name, never display text: one side renders a catalog string from it and",
    "the other writes it into a report. A `proceed` case carries no reason.",
    "",
    "`fields` names what a form fill targets. Absent means the caller cannot",
    "name them, which a lock covering ALL fields is still decidable against.",
    "",
    "`typed` names the caller's own half of `fields`; the rest is what the",
    "document's own calculation order would recompute as a result. When a lock",
    "bites ONLY that computed half the refusal is `indirect`, because a user",
    "told \"Total is locked\" after typing into \"Item 1\" has been told nothing."
  ],
